WEBVTT

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:16.760
Amazing! Amazing!

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:20.370
So this thing, this Entei, 
is going to be mine now?

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:23.960
Does it bother you that this 
Buranki has experienced defeat?

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:28.190
Not really. Entei doesn't need 
Bubuki users for limbs, right?

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:29.670
I actually like that about it!

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:32.970
No problems with any values at the moment.

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:35.730
<i>Problems? Of course there 
won't be any problems!</i>

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:39.090
Kaoruko, I'd like you to use 
that power to protect the world

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:40.970
from those unsightly Buranki.

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:43.560
Yeah, of course I will. It only makes sense.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:46.100
That's my duty as a genius heart user.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.550
Thank you.

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:50.320
In that case, I'd also like you

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:53.280
to take care of a certain traitor.

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:55.610
Traitor?

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:56.860
What do you mean?

00:00:56.860 --> 00:00:58.800
It saddens me to say it,

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:01.070
but there is one among us here

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:05.120
in Demokratia who intends to turn against me.

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:09.880
I want you to hunt down and 
eliminate that Bubuki user.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:14.770
The traitor is a Bubuki user?

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:16.510
<i>Ironically, yes.</i>

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:20.760
<i>But for one with natural talent such 
as yourself, it will be a simple task.</i>

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:22.640
Th-That's right!

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:28.360
For the genius Kaoruko-sama, a measly 
traitor or two is nothing!

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.160
<b><i>BUBUKI/BURANKI</i></b>

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:44.160
<b>The Gentle Giants of the Galaxy</b>

00:01:58.590 --> 00:01:59.180
BURANKI

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:02.850
BURANKI

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:06.640
BURANKI

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:26.540
Kazuki

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:26.540
Kaoruko

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:57.440
<b><i>BUBUKI/BURANKI</i></b>

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:57.440
<b>The Gentle Giants of the Galaxy</b>

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:59.030
<b><i>BUBUKI/BURANKI</i></b>

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:59.030
<b>The Gentle Giants of the Galaxy</b>

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:02.840
So where is this boat of Matobai's?

00:03:03.230 --> 00:03:05.740
I don't see a boat anywhere.

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:14.570
<i>Sorry to make you wait.</i>

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:19.840
This is...

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:21.990
...one hell of an airship.

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:25.660
Reoko-sama bought it a while back.

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:27.110
It's a flying boat constructed in

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:31.100
Germany for the transport 
of Buranki, the Argo Gaura.

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:33.810
Argo Gaura

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:34.210
With this thing, it's just a 
quick hop to the western coast

00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:38.070
of France, where Reoko-sama 
is being confined.

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:39.780
Confined?

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:41.700
Who has Reoko, exactly?

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:44.640
Guy Barville Abeille...

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:46.660
The president of Demokratia.

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:48.600
That name comes up again?

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:50.830
What is this Demokratia thing, anyway?

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:53.840
Demokratia is a supranational organization

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:56.580
that's trying to take hold of all rights

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:59.100
to everything involving Buranki.

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:02.030
Guy is the leader of Maxim and his gang,

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:05.430
and Azuma, he's your 
sister's patron, as well.

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:06.760
Kaoruko's...

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:09.330
And that Guy bastard is apparently

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:13.920
interested in Reoko-sama's body, 
because it's connected to Entei.

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:20.400
So I ask you...

00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:24.200
Please lend me your strength, 
so I can rescue Reoko-sama.

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:28.450
Okay, we will, Matobai-san.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:32.940
Thanks, Azuma. I owe you.

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:34.210
In return...

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:37.620
I want you to help me rescue Kaoruko.

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:40.420
Kaoruko's been deceived by this Guy person.

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:44.580
All right. It's a done deal, then.

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:54.380
It really sucks though, 
huh, Old Man Matobai?

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:02.900
So you were the only one to survive?

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:08.050
Huh? Whoa, hang on.
What are you talking about?

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:11.480
The other three, well...

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:13.370
They all died, right?

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:14.900
Three?

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:18.900
You mean Tsuwabuki, Hazama, and Souya?

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:22.760
Those guys are alive and damned well!

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:24.130
What?!

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:26.850
How the hell are you alive, anyway?!

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:30.100
Didn't you get shot by Arabashiri 
on Treasure Island?!

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:32.430
Oh, that?

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:36.530
Souya stopped the bleeding 
right away with his Rinzu.

00:05:36.530 --> 00:05:38.400
It still smarts, though.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:41.040
He fell into the sea, but he's fine.

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:42.620
Hmph.

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:44.900
What about Uncle Akihito?

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:49.540
He's currently carrying out 
a plan to rescue Reoko-sama.

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:52.110
Damn it! I was worried for nothing!

00:05:52.110 --> 00:05:54.590
Worried? Worried about... C'mon, Kinoa...

00:05:54.590 --> 00:05:57.150
You'll see them soon enough.

00:05:57.550 --> 00:06:00.880
Of course, Hazama might be 
a different story, though.

00:06:04.850 --> 00:06:05.830
All right!

00:06:05.830 --> 00:06:08.210
Let's get moving, then!

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:32.240
Elder Brother...

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:34.110
You are unhurt?

00:06:34.110 --> 00:06:37.250
Y-Yes, I'm completely fine.

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:40.050
I'm as alive as can be, Elder Brother!

00:06:43.350 --> 00:06:45.140
Ignat and Dersu, are you okay, too?

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:47.010
Elder Brother?!

00:06:47.010 --> 00:06:48.700
E-E-E-Elder Brother!

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:50.990
Why are you two so surprised?

00:06:50.990 --> 00:06:53.880
Elder Brother, pardon me a moment.
Are you feverish?

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:01.100
More importantly...

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:05.270
Do you all remember the battle between 
Zampaza and the Buranki Oubu?

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:08.740
We were fighting a Buranki?

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:14.060
Yes, but with your consciousnesses 
sealed off by Guy,

00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:18.290
in order to draw out Zampaza's powers, 
as well as my own, to the fullest.

00:07:19.550 --> 00:07:23.440
But in reality, not only did 
it not draw out those powers,

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:26.380
but I was defeated by Kazuki Azuma's Oubu.

00:07:26.730 --> 00:07:28.980
Which means, if the limbs 
lack functioning minds,

00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:32.010
the heart can't demonstrate 
its full power, either.

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:40.460
I need all of you, with your minds intact.

00:07:41.010 --> 00:07:42.980
I finally realized that.

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:47.960
Elder Brother...

00:07:57.320 --> 00:07:59.370
We need to move before the sun sets.

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:02.080
Elder Brother, I see someone!

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:03.960
I'll ask them the way to the city!

00:08:04.610 --> 00:08:05.720
Right...

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:07.800
Be careful, Lyu.

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:08.750
I will!

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:13.880
Thank you.

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:17.090
Why thank me?

00:08:17.090 --> 00:08:24.940
I never dreamed the day would 
come when you'd call me by name.

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:40.040
Dersu!

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:42.290
Dersu! Dersu!

00:08:42.590 --> 00:08:43.610
Dersu!

00:08:56.490 --> 00:08:58.680
It's what they call the taiga.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:01.140
Pretty soon all the green will be gone,

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:03.060
and it'll be covered in ice and snow.

00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:07.690
With this flying boat, we can reach 
the ends of the earth in no time.

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:10.240
Hats off to science, huh?

00:09:20.710 --> 00:09:22.260
Hey, come on!

00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:24.790
I thought you said a little 
blizzard like this was nothing!

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:28.460
The GPS compass is all out of whack,

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:31.730
and now we're being sucked in 
by some giant mass of Rinzu!

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:38.970
You guys! Grab onto something, anything!

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:52.120
Ow...

00:09:52.620 --> 00:09:54.640
You guys all right?!

00:09:54.640 --> 00:09:56.390
Whoa! Sorry, Hiiragi!

00:09:57.660 --> 00:09:59.200
Sorry, Shizuru!

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:00.320
Someone's...

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:03.370
Someone's out there! A kid's passed out!

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:10.260
How's she doing?

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:12.750
I don't see any injuries. 
I think she's okay.

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:16.260
C'mon, let's get back to the boat!

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:18.970
Even with our bodies enveloped in Rinzu,

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:21.330
in a blizzard like this, we'll freeze solid!

00:10:21.750 --> 00:10:24.600
Shizuru, what's up? Something wrong?

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:46.250
What's this place?

00:10:50.600 --> 00:10:53.130
Dersu is already dead.

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:54.390
Oh, no...

00:10:55.790 --> 00:10:59.970
Who is targeting us, and why?

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:02.550
It's a Bubuki user.

00:11:02.550 --> 00:11:07.110
When it happened, a bullet 
shot through Amba's barrier.

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:08.600
A bullet?

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:10.980
The little rock girl from Yaponiya, then?

00:11:11.580 --> 00:11:12.800
I don't know.

00:11:13.250 --> 00:11:16.580
Either way, it's too dangerous to stay here.

00:11:16.580 --> 00:11:20.100
But Lyudmila isn't back yet...

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:22.240
We'll search for her as we move.

00:11:23.380 --> 00:11:24.460
Amba...

00:11:25.110 --> 00:11:28.330
I'm sorry, but we'll have to 
leave you and Dersu here.

00:11:29.030 --> 00:11:31.000
We'll be back as soon 
as we defeat the enemy.

00:11:31.470 --> 00:11:34.250
Just wait here with him until then.

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:51.700
Oh, good. You're awake.

00:11:57.950 --> 00:11:59.880
Is that a Buranki?

00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:01.800
Which country is it from?

00:12:09.310 --> 00:12:11.710
A purple... Oubu?

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:13.240
Duroc.

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:18.920
Thank you for saving the girl, Yuk.

00:12:19.440 --> 00:12:20.510
I am grateful.

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:21.050
Huh?!

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:23.550
The Buranki... talked?!

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:33.060
<b>Episode 16
The Hunter's Bullet</b>

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:33.060
<b><i>BUBUKI BURANKI
The Gentle Giants
 of the Galaxy</i></b>

00:12:35.350 --> 00:12:37.610
<b><i>BUBUKI BURANKI</i></b>

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:37.610
<b>The Gentle Giants of the Galaxy</b>

00:12:46.290 --> 00:12:47.620
Long ago,

00:12:48.260 --> 00:12:50.750
when we arrived on this planet,

00:12:50.750 --> 00:12:55.460
we were already facing the 
twilight of our race.

00:12:56.260 --> 00:13:02.010
The organ you refer to as the 
"brain" had ceased to function.

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:07.590
In order to survive, we divided 
our bodies into five parts,

00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:12.640
and looked to you humans, beings with 
developed brains, as our masters.

00:13:14.920 --> 00:13:17.050
And that's what Bubuki are...

00:13:17.050 --> 00:13:18.060
Yes.

00:13:18.430 --> 00:13:22.900
They are the form we take to accompany 
and protect our human masters.

00:13:22.900 --> 00:13:25.210
In this smaller form,

00:13:25.210 --> 00:13:28.950
we are able to survive by 
communicating with the brains

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:31.120
of our human masters.

00:13:37.930 --> 00:13:39.130
However...

00:13:39.130 --> 00:13:42.090
Those who chose not to mingle with humans

00:13:42.090 --> 00:13:45.220
returned to the sky,
where their brains decayed,

00:13:47.030 --> 00:13:48.820
falling off along with their heads.

00:13:48.820 --> 00:13:51.850
And that's what the headless Buranki are?

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:55.510
Soon, my brain will also decay,

00:13:56.080 --> 00:13:57.880
and like my family,

00:13:57.880 --> 00:14:01.860
I will become a being with no 
consciousness that simply walks about.

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:04.840
But how are you able to move?

00:14:04.840 --> 00:14:08.950
Didn't Migiwa-san stop the hearts 
of all Buranki on Earth?

00:14:09.370 --> 00:14:13.410
Only the hearts of the Buranki 
who contracted with humans.

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:17.690
Only when we choose to coexist with a human,

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:21.340
do our hearts leave our bodies.

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:23.880
It is the proof of a contract 
between human and Buranki.

00:14:24.520 --> 00:14:27.410
Those are the hearts that 
you humans possess.

00:14:29.430 --> 00:14:31.800
Proof of a contract...

00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:46.800
Ugh, I can't take it! 
It's way too damn cold!

00:14:48.970 --> 00:14:50.990
Hot! Hot! Hot!

00:14:51.520 --> 00:14:52.990
Hey, it's a hot spring!

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:54.080
What?!

00:14:57.590 --> 00:14:59.760
K-Kinoa! What are you doing?!

00:14:59.760 --> 00:15:01.080
It's a hot spring!

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:03.890
Azuma, Hiiragi! You guys turn around!

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:12.760
Buying swimsuits in Taiwan 
was the right call, Kogane!

00:15:13.290 --> 00:15:15.100
Oh, it was nothing.

00:15:16.790 --> 00:15:18.230
But, Shizuru-chan,

00:15:18.230 --> 00:15:21.000
I'm impressed you knew there 
was a hot spring here.

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:23.230
C-C-C-C-Can't...

00:15:23.790 --> 00:15:28.120
You two, put on your swimsuits 
before you step outside.

00:15:28.120 --> 00:15:30.030
There's a hot spring beside us.

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:30.930
For real?!

00:15:30.930 --> 00:15:32.160
For real.

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:36.660
Man, this is bliss.

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:42.560
Poke, poke...

00:15:38.770 --> 00:15:43.540
Hey, Duroc-san, what's your 
relation to this kid?

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:46.630
I have known this girl 
since she was very young.

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:50.840
She would often come to me, 
along with her father.

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:55.570
Perhaps they thought I was 
what the humans call a "god."

00:15:56.070 --> 00:15:58.950
But after some time,

00:15:58.950 --> 00:16:01.600
she started to come to me alone.

00:16:01.860 --> 00:16:04.860
Her dad stopped coming? Does that mean...

00:16:04.860 --> 00:16:06.190
We're sorry.

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:07.860
No, it's okay.

00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:09.860
I have Duroc with me.

00:16:10.250 --> 00:16:14.950
Earlier, when you saw that she 
was safe, you were happy.

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:17.870
Happy? I was?

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:22.250
Yes. So much that it made me happy, too.

00:16:22.820 --> 00:16:27.280
I see... I was happy.

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:31.150
Hey, can I ask you something?

00:16:31.150 --> 00:16:34.310
What did you guys come to Earth 
to do in the first place?

00:16:34.310 --> 00:16:38.100
You didn't want to destroy 
the planet, did you?

00:16:38.760 --> 00:16:43.350
Are you not the ones who are 
destroying this planet?

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:51.560
You kill, steal, and change the face 
of this planet as it suits you.

00:16:51.560 --> 00:16:54.320
Is that not what you humans do?

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:01.930
Ignat, does something seem strange to you?

00:17:01.930 --> 00:17:03.760
I can't sense the enemy's bloodlust at all.

00:17:03.760 --> 00:17:05.040
Yes, it does.

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:10.000
E-Elder Brother!

00:17:19.440 --> 00:17:20.670
Maxim-sama!

00:17:20.670 --> 00:17:23.060
Damn it! Where's the shooter?

00:17:26.920 --> 00:17:28.550
Elder Brother, you're bleeding!

00:17:28.550 --> 00:17:29.230
Don't!

00:17:37.870 --> 00:17:39.010
Ignat!

00:17:39.580 --> 00:17:41.740
Elder Brother! Elder Brother!

00:17:42.130 --> 00:17:43.410
Lyu! Are you okay?!

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:44.410
Yes!

00:17:45.980 --> 00:17:47.960
Ignat! Ignat!

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:51.960
He was protecting me.

00:18:01.420 --> 00:18:03.890
No... No!

00:18:06.710 --> 00:18:09.310
She's still brainwashed?

00:18:11.830 --> 00:18:14.860
This was all set up from the start?

00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:13.600
No!

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:18.850
Stop! Stop! Stop!

00:18:18.850 --> 00:18:21.370
So this is why he gave us that new power,

00:18:21.370 --> 00:18:24.410
even though he knew I had 
treacherous intentions?

00:18:26.120 --> 00:18:29.180
And once his "experiment" was over,

00:18:29.180 --> 00:18:31.590
he had no further need for us?

00:18:30.760 --> 00:18:32.380
Stop!

00:18:43.340 --> 00:18:46.170
Guy... You'll pay!

00:18:46.170 --> 00:18:47.480
You'll pay for this!

00:18:58.810 --> 00:19:02.290
The rats exterminated themselves 
with their own hands.

00:19:02.290 --> 00:19:04.030
Truly splendid work.

00:19:04.030 --> 00:19:06.610
And now we have the data proving the

00:19:06.610 --> 00:19:09.670
Buranki Zampaza can function 
with only a heart user.

00:19:09.670 --> 00:19:12.760
Those vile rats, killing their own family.

00:19:21.030 --> 00:19:22.980
When separated from Entei,

00:19:22.980 --> 00:19:26.350
you don't even have the 
strength to pick up a glass.

00:19:26.930 --> 00:19:28.850
How truly pitiful.

00:19:31.990 --> 00:19:37.290
Exterminating the Bubuki users 
is but a small part of our plan.

00:19:37.290 --> 00:19:39.610
My true objective is...

00:19:44.550 --> 00:19:49.130
Lives take lives in order to stay alive.

00:19:49.130 --> 00:19:53.380
This is necessary in order to survive.

00:19:54.150 --> 00:19:59.510
But you humans kill other 
species for no reason.

00:19:59.920 --> 00:20:02.890
Sometimes even your own families.

00:20:03.440 --> 00:20:05.970
It is a chronic disease of your species.

00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:07.220
Chronic?

00:20:07.690 --> 00:20:09.670
A disease that can't be cured.

00:20:09.670 --> 00:20:10.730
Thank you.

00:20:11.740 --> 00:20:12.520
Duroc...

00:20:12.520 --> 00:20:15.820
Hey! You guys were awake?!

00:20:16.810 --> 00:20:21.340
Duroc, that may be a part of human nature 
that we can't do anything about.

00:20:21.340 --> 00:20:24.860
But I believe humans can change.

00:20:24.860 --> 00:20:27.200
I'm sure that in the future...

00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:30.060
That's right. Humans can change.

00:20:30.060 --> 00:20:31.540
I believe that, too.

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:34.590
In the future, you say.

00:20:41.320 --> 00:20:43.510
Please tell us, Duroc.

00:20:43.840 --> 00:20:48.060
Why didn't you contract with a human?

00:20:48.970 --> 00:20:52.240
For the same reason your mother, Migiwa,

00:20:52.240 --> 00:20:57.560
stopped the hearts of all Buranki on Earth.

00:20:57.860 --> 00:20:59.010
My mom?

00:20:59.450 --> 00:21:01.270
It is clear to me.

00:21:01.740 --> 00:21:04.240
You are the son of Akira and Migiwa.

00:21:05.570 --> 00:21:09.790
Migiwa is the human I am closest to.

00:21:09.790 --> 00:21:11.870
I would even call her a friend.

00:21:12.350 --> 00:21:15.000
My mom is... your friend?

00:21:15.420 --> 00:21:18.480
Gentle child who cares for his mother...

00:21:18.480 --> 00:21:20.250
Migiwa is alive.

00:21:20.680 --> 00:21:22.750
You will see her soon.

00:21:23.650 --> 00:21:27.910
Duroc, what exactly are you Buranki, anyway?

00:21:29.240 --> 00:21:31.300
We are servants.

00:21:31.300 --> 00:21:36.810
No more than loyal servants to 
the Great One of the beginning.

00:21:36.810 --> 00:21:39.190
Great One?

00:21:52.300 --> 00:21:56.670
So you boys didn't get in the hot spring?

00:21:56.670 --> 00:22:00.780
We didn't have a choice! 
They wouldn't let us in!

00:22:06.320 --> 00:22:08.250
Don't you laugh!
